B.Uh=new A.a5("Which standardized assessment tool is most commonly used to quantify stroke severity and guide treatment decisions?",B.M9,1,"The NIH Stroke Scale (NIHSS) is the standard tool for quantifying stroke severity acutely. It scores 0-42, assessing consciousness, gaze, visual fields, facial palsy, motor function, ataxia, sensory, language, dysarthria, and extinction/inattention.")
B.ON=s(["140/90 mmHg","160/100 mmHg","180/105 mmHg","220/120 mmHg"],t.s)
B.Uf=new A.a5("Blood pressure management in the first 24 hours after tPA administration requires maintaining BP below which threshold?",B.ON,2,"After tPA administration, blood pressure must be maintained below 180/105 mmHg to reduce the risk of hemorrhagic transformation. In patients NOT receiving tPA, permissive hypertension up to 220/120 is generally allowed.")
