B.TF=new A.a5("The apparent rise in stroke incidence in the early 1980s is best explained by which of the following?",B.M_,2,'The ~17% spike in stroke incidence in the early 1980s is a data artifact caused by the widespread availability of CT scanners. Previously, many strokes were misdiagnosed as "sudden spells" or "senility." Better detection increased apparent incidence without a true increase in events.')
B.MO=s(["Third","Fourth","Fifth","Sixth"],t.s)
B.Tr=new A.a5("Stroke is currently ranked as which leading cause of death in the United States?",B.MO,2,"Stroke is the 5th leading cause of death in the US, behind: (1) heart disease, (2) cancer, (3) chronic lower respiratory disease (COPD), and (4) accidents/unintentional injuries. It previously held the 3rd position.")
